// Exercise E2 "Creating sheet metal parts" (P3I.4 part: steps 3–6 and 9–11; slides
// `ex2-creating-sheet-metal-parts/step-*.png`) on a stand-in: the profile on Front is the
// exercise's (15 high walls, 125 wide) with the R35 arc replaced by a trapezoid of lines (a sheet
// metal Extrude in cadrs bends only between lines; the arc's ends meet the lines at an angle).
// Step 3: Sheet metal model, Extrude 80 mm, 1 mm thick, bend radius 1 mm. Step 4: Flange on the
// two back edges (the left base and the left wall), Inner, 8 mm: one plane, mitred at the
// corner. Step 5: Partial flange, Per chain, Hold adjacent edges, Blind 10 mm. Step 6: Hem on
// the two flanges' top edges: Straight, Flattened, 5 mm, In place, Simple. Steps 9–10: Flange 2
// on the right base's front edge (15 mm, as high as the right wall) and Flange 3 on the right
// wall's top edge (10 mm). Step 11: Make joint between Flange 2's side and the right wall's
// front edge: Rip, Butt joint – Direction 1.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(30),
        Custom("sketch front chain 0 15 0 0 40 0 52 10 73 10 85 0 125 0 125 15"),
        Wait(5),
        Key("Shift+7"),
        Wait(40),
        Click(ui("sheet-metal-model")),
        WaitFor("sheet-metal-model-dialog"),
